<h1><span lang="EN-GB">New Point</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="bullet"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">T</span>his command is accessible from</i> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Datuming &gt; Point</b></span><span class="Path">,</span> by using the shortcut <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Shift + Alt + 1</b></span> <span class="Shortcut">or by choosing the</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Point tab</b></span> <span class="Shortcut">in the</span> <span class="Shortcut" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Datum creation</u></span> <span class="Shortcut">mode (if it is currently active).</span></p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description</b></span>: New Point command creates new datum point by one of the 7 available methods. Here below these methods are explained followed by examples.</p>
<h2><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">M</span></i><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">ethods:</span></i></h2>
<p class="sub-head"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">Interactive</span></i></p>
<p><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><img src="Images/new_point_interactive.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">: standard point construction using one of the available 4</span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">definition</span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">methods (pick from viewport is enabled by default). For more details about the define section, see <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_point.htm">Define Point</a>.</span></i></p>
<p class="Example" style="font-style:normal; text-decoration:underline;"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></i></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP936742772" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/InteractivePoint.gif" width="469px" height="547px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="whs6">&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Intersection of 2 lines</p>
<p><img src="Images/new_point_2lines.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""> : This method includes definition of 2 construction lines. <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">For more details about the define section, see <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_line.htm">Define Line</a>.</span></i></p>
<p id="p4"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>H</b>ow it works</i></span></i>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip5">
<p class="steps" id="p5">The user defines two lines one by one.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip5">
<p class="steps" id="p5">Depending on the line positions, the result point can be:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip5">
<p class="bullet" id="p5">intersection of the lines (in case both lines lie in a plane)</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip5">
<p class="bullet" id="p5">middle of the transversal (in case of crossed lines)</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CImportant-Ip5">
<p class="Important" id="p5">In case of parallel lines, no result point can be created.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="p18"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">C</span></i>hanges of all values can be applied at any time.</p>
<p id="P1" class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for point by 2 crossed lines</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP238158298" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/PointByTwoLinesCr.gif" width="680px" height="549px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Point on line</p>
<p><img src="Images/new_point_on_line.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""> : This method includes definition of a line and adjustment of point position on it. <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">For more details about the define section, see <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_line.htm">Define Line</a>.</span></i></p>
<p id="p2"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>H</b>ow it works</i></span></i>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip3">
<p class="steps" id="p3">The user defines a line.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip3">
<p class="steps" id="p3">The point position on line should be adjusted. There are different possibilities available:</p>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip3">
<p class="bullet" id="p3">Button <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>First point</b></span> enabled - the result point will be the start point of the selected line.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip3">
<p class="bullet" id="p3">Button <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mid point</b></span> enabled - the result point will be the middle point of the selected line.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip3">
<p class="bullet" id="p3">Button <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Last point</b></span> enabled - the result point will be the end point of the selected line.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip3">
<p class="bullet" id="p3">Value <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X mm from the first point</b></span> - the result point will lie on the line at X mm from the start point in axis direction.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip3">
<p class="bullet" id="p3">Value <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X length ratio from the first point</b></span> - the result point will lie on the line at the X length ratio from the first point in axis direction.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li style="list-style:none; display:inline;">
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet-Ip3">
<p class="bullet" id="p3">If the checkbox Inverse direction is enabled, then the result point will be created at the given position on the line, but in inverse axis direction.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="p12"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">C</span></i>hanges of all values can be applied at any time.</p>
<p id="p3" class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a6" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP237117797" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/PointOnLine.gif" width="415px" height="553px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p class="Use">This method is very useful when needed to create mid point between two circles or two spheres.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a7" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for two circles</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP226752658" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/PointBy2Circles.gif" width="626px" height="595px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Intersection of 3 planes</p>
<p><img src="Images/new_point_3planes.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""> : This method includes definition of 3 construction planes. <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">For more details about the define section, see <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_plane.htm">Define Plane</a>.</span></i></p>
<p id="p6"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>H</b>ow it works</i></span></i>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip7">
<p class="steps" id="p7">The user defines three planes one by one.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip7">
<p class="steps" id="p7">The result point is intersection between the planes.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip7">
<p class="steps" id="p7">If two or three planes are parallel, then result point can not be created.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="p13"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">C</span></i>hanges of all values can be applied at any time.</p>
<p class="Example" id="p14" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP296380941" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/PointByThreePlanes.gif" width="743px" height="620px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Intersection of line and object</p>
<p><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b><img src="Images/new_point_plane_line.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></b></span> : This method includes definition of 2 construction entities: line and object (cone, plane, sphere, or cylinder). <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">For more details about the define section, see <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_line.htm">Define Line</a> for line definition and <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_cone.htm">Define Cone</a>, &#160;<a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_plane.htm">Define Plane</a>, <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_sphere.htm">Define Sphere</a>, and <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_cylinder.htm">Define Cylinder</a> for object definition.</span></i></p>
<p id="p8"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>H</b>ow it works</i></span></i>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip9">
<p class="steps" id="p9">The user defines a line and an object. The type of object is selected from the following drop-down list:<br>
<br>
<img src="Images/new_point_object_selection.gif" width="273px" height="162px" border="0" class="img_whs12" alt=""></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip9">
<p class="steps" id="p9">The result point is intersection between both entities.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip9">
<p class="steps" id="p9">If the line and the object don't intersect (or the line is parallel to the plane/cylinder's axis or the line lies on the plane/cylinder's slant surface/cone's slant surface), then result point can not be created.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip9">
<p class="steps" id="p9">In case of volumetric entities (cone, sphere, and cylinder) and two intersections the result point is the first cross point between the line and the object along the line direction.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="p15"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">C</span></i>hanges of all values can be applied at any time.</p>
<p class="Example" id="p16" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a4" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for point by line and sphere</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP225404521" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/PointBySphereLine.gif" width="644px" height="555px" border="0" class="img_whs13" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Point projection</p>
<p><img src="Images/new_point_projection.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""> : This method includes definition of 2 construction entity types: projection entity (point, circle or sphere) and entity to project on it (line or plane).</p>
<p id="p10"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>How it works</b></i></span>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip11">
<p class="steps" id="p11">The user selects entity type for the source (projected) entity using the drop-down list (in the first tab)</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip17">
<p class="steps" id="p17">A particular entity of the selected type (plane, circle or sphere for this method) should be defined. For more details about construction entity definitions, see <i><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_point.htm">Define Point</a>,</span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_circle.htm">Define Circle</a>,</span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_sphere.htm">Define Sphere</a></span></i><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">.</span></i></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip17">
<p class="steps" id="p17"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">Same procedure (steps 1 and 2) to be followed for the target entity (entity to project on it).</span></i> <i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:normal;">For more details about the define section, see</span> </i><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_line.htm">Define Line</a> and</span></i> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US"><a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_plane.htm">Define Plane</a>.</span></i></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="p19" class="whs6"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">Alternative way of steps 1,2 and 3 is:</span></i></p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip20">
<p class="steps" id="p20">Enable the option 'Pick from screen' in the drop-down list (in the first tab)</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip21">
<p class="steps" id="p21">Select and define simultaneously the type and values for the construction entity. This procedure is very suitable for quick selection of predefined datums.</p>
</li>
<li style="font-style:normal;" class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip21">
<p class="steps" id="p21"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">Same procedure (steps 1 and 2) to be followed for the target entity.</span></i></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="p22">Common for both procedures:</p>
<ol start="4">
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip23">
<p class="steps" id="p23">The result point represents the projection of the source entity (point, sphere centre or circle centre) on the target entity (line or plane).</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip23">
<p class="steps" id="p23">If the source entity lies on the target one, then the result point will be identical to the construction one.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p id="p24">Changes of all values can be applied at any time.</p>
<p id="p24" class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span style="font-style:normal;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a5" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for circle projection on a line</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP171378868" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/PointByProjection.gif" width="689px" height="548px" border="0" class="img_whs14" alt=""></p>
</div>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p class="sub-head">Intersection of 2 circles</p>
<p><img src="Images/new_point_2circles.gif" width="32px" height="29px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""> : This method includes definition of 2 construction circles. <i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">For more details about the define section, see <a href="../Working_with_Data/Descriptions/define_circle.htm">Define Circle</a>.</span></i></p>
<p id="p25"><i><span lang="EN-US" style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>H</b>ow it works</i></span></i>:</p>
<ol>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip26">
<p class="steps" id="p26">The user defines two circles one by one.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Csteps-Ip27">
<p class="steps" id="p27">The result point is intersection between the two circles. There are two cross points. Press <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Toggle solution</b></span> button to switch between them.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="Warning" id="p30">In case of non-intersected circles, no result point can be created. If the two circles are not co-planar the result is unpredictable.</p>
<p id="p31"><i style="font-style:normal;"><span lang="EN-US">C</span></i>hanges of all values can be applied at any time.</p>
<p class="Example" id="p32" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a8" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example for point by 2 crossed circles</a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP289373920" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<p><img src="Examples/PointBy2CrossedCircles.gif" width="556px" height="546px" border="0" class="img_whs15" alt=""></p>
</div>
